# Frame by Frame design

Read `docs/design-system.md` (v2, "Kinetoscope") before changing UI. Tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css`; never write a raw hex in a component.

- Five styles, five layers (§1): Victorian owns titles, rules and frames; pop art owns buttons, chips, badges and checkboxes; retro-futurist HUD owns mono readouts; aurora owns header bands, the hero and the ceremony; film owns the filmstrip and grain. A style outside its layer is a spec change.
- One hue per meaning: teal (`--accent-primary`) is action; brass (`--accent-warm`, `--brass-fill`) is progress and completion only, never on links, buttons, filters, nav or ornaments.
- Abril Fatface is weight 400 only with `font-synthesis: none`. No faked small caps.
- Ornaments, halftone, HUD frames and aurora are CSS, not JSX. Halftone never sits under text.
- Pop shadows are a pseudo-element moved with `transform`; never animate `box-shadow`.

- Breakpoints are `360` (floor), `640`, `768` (bottom tabs swap to the left rail), `1024`, and `1440`. No horizontal scroll at 360px. Body text stays at least 16px on mobile. Page gutters are 16px, then 24px from 640px, then 48px from 1024px.
- Touch targets are at least 48×48px, with at least 8px between them.
- Animate `transform` and `opacity` only. Hover never uses `scale`. `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` collapses durations.
- Grain never shares a stacking layer with text, and `--grain-opacity` is `0` in light mode.
- Focus is `outline: 2px solid var(--accent-primary); outline-offset: 2px`. Never remove the outline without a replacement.
- Decorative canvases and grain are `aria-hidden`. An image that carries meaning has a specific `alt`. An image that is pure decoration has `alt=""`.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — a hover that reflows the library grid */
.card:hover { transform: scale(1.04); }

/* ✅ GOOD — color and border only */
.card:hover { background: var(--bg-hover); }
```
